# Numbered G/M macros: call directly (hard stop)

RepRapFirmware loads **`0:/sys/M####.g`** / **`0:/sys/G####.g`** as numbered meta commands. Release sync flattens [`macros/`](../../macros/) into **`0:/sys/`**, so **`M6520`**, **`G6503`**, **`M4006`**, etc. run as themselves.

## Why not `M98`

1. **`M98` reserves `P` for the filename** — you cannot pass nested **`P`** (e.g. result index). That caused the probe U-chain abort: `M6520: Result index parameter P is required`.
2. Extra path indirection is unnecessary when the file is already on `0:/sys/`.

## Rules for every agent (mandatory)

1. **Do not** write `M98 P"M….g"` or `M98 P"G….g"` (any path whose basename is `M`/`G` + digits, optional `.N`, + `.g`).
2. **Do** invoke the numbered command directly and pass real parameters:

```gcode
; ❌ BAD — M98; P cannot be a nested param
M98 P"M6520.g" P{var.pSlot} W{param.U} X Y

; ✅ GOOD — meta command; P is M6520's result index
M6520 P{var.pSlot} W{param.U} X Y

; ❌ BAD — named helper; second P is still stolen by M98
M98 P"nxt-probe-sensor-wait.g" P1

; ✅ GOOD — named helper; other letters are passed through
M98 P"nxt-probe-sensor-wait.g" Q1
M98 P"nxt-wcs-apply.g" I{var.pSlot} W{var.wcs}

; ❌ BAD
M98 P"M4006.g"

; ✅ GOOD
M4006
```

3. **Before** claiming macro work done, run: `node dist/check-m98-numbered-meta.mjs` — must exit 0. Named helpers without a nested **`P`** are OK. The checker also fails `M98 P"nxt-….g" P…`.
4. Prefer **`M98`** only for **named** helpers (`nxt-*.g`, board packs, etc.), not for codes listed in [`GCODE.md`](../../GCODE.md).

